{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The requirement has two obligations. Each bundled skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow. That workflow must be ordered steps. Both apply to every skill, so each site upholds them on its own. The test in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` checks them across all skills.\n\n**Test: `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]`**\n- It loops over every skill in `SKILLS`.\n- It asserts that the first `## ` heading in each `SKILL.md` is exactly `## Workflow`. That covers \"before any other section\".\n- It parses the Workflow section with `workflow_steps`. The helper is reached from the marked test, so it needs no reference of its own.\n- It asserts at least two numbered steps, and that the numbers run 1..n in order. That covers \"ordered steps\".\n- It checks the exact heading and the numbering, so a skill with a reordered section or a gap or duplicate in the numbering would fail.\n- The set of skills it covers is complete. `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_are_five_skill_directories_each_home_to_its_topics]` asserts that the directories under `assets/skills` are exactly `SKILLS`. It also checks the front matter of each `SKILL.md`.\n\n**Site query `skills`.**\n- Running it matched exactly the five `SKILL.md` files, each by its front matter: `habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`.\n- The markdown files under `references/` have no front matter, so they are rightly not selected. They are not skills.\n- A search of `assets/skills` for `## ` headings found no other skill-like file that the query misses.\n- The match snippet (front matter followed by a heading) and the no_match snippet (a heading with no front matter) show both what the query selects and what it leaves out.\n\n**Gaps.** None found. There are no acknowledgments, and none were needed.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
